  "title": "Be Cautious About Assuming Others Agree with You",
  "description": "Be cautious about assuming others agree with you. Here’s how: - Ask instead of assuming: Check in with others about their opinions before concluding they match yours. - Look for diversity: Actively seek out different perspectives to challenge your assumptions. - Be curious: Treat disagreements as opportunities to learn, not threats. Example: If you believe everyone on your team supports a decision, ask, “How do you feel about this?” to confirm.",
